{"name":"Herb Garden","hex":"#e9f3e1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"herb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant whose stem is not woody and does not persist beyond each growing season.","Grass; herbage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/herb"},{"term":"garden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An outdoor area containing one or more types of plants, usually plants grown for food or ornamental purposes.","Such an ornamental place to which the public have access."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grow plants in a garden; to create or maintain a garden.","Of a batsman, to inspect and tap the pitch lightly with the bat so as to smooth out small rough patches and irregularities."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kitchen garden","blocks":[{"text":"The traditional kitchen garden, vegetable garden, also known as a potager or in Scotland a kailyaird, is a space separate from the rest of the residential garden – the ornamental plants and lawn areas – used for growing edible plants, especially historically. In large country houses, the kitchen garden was a segregated area, normally rectangular and enclosed by a wall or hedge."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Jardin_potager_001.JPG/330px-Jardin_potager_001.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kitchen_garden","wikidata":"Q624114"},{"title":"Herb","blocks":[{"text":"Herbs are a widely distributed and widespread group of plants, excluding vegetables, with savory or aromatic properties that are used for flavoring and garnishing food, for medicinal purposes, or for fragrances. Culinary use typically distinguishes herbs from spices. Herbs generally refers to the leafy green or flowering parts of a plant, while spices are usually dried and produced from other parts of the plant, including seeds, bark, roots and fruits."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Garden_of_herbs.jpg/330px-Garden_of_herbs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herb","wikidata":"Q207123"},{"title":"Garden","blocks":[{"text":"A garden is a planned space, usually outdoors, set aside for the cultivation, display, and enjoyment of plants and other forms of nature. The single feature identifying even the wildest wild garden is control. The garden can incorporate both natural and artificial materials."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg/330px-Brooklyn_Botanic_Garden_New_York_May_2015_010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garden","wikidata":"Q1107656"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Vegetable_garden_at_Ham_House_Estate_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4530.jpg/500px-Vegetable_garden_at_Ham_House_Estate_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4530.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Vegetable_garden_at_Ham_House_Estate_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4530.jpg/500px-Vegetable_garden_at_Ham_House_Estate_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4530.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Walled 17th-century kitchen garden at Ham House near London, with orangery in the distance.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVegetable_garden_at_Ham_House_Estate_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4530.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/HerbalPatch_Lippensgoed_Bulskampveld.jpg/500px-HerbalPatch_Lippensgoed_Bulskampveld.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/HerbalPatch_Lippensgoed_Bulskampveld.jpg/1280px-He